        {
          "kind": "section",
          "heading": "One clock for every wait",
          "body": "`minutes_until`, which words the error message (\"try again in 12 minutes\"), read the clock on its own. Both now call `unix_now`, so the message and the hold agree on what *now* is. `retry_after_from` takes the clock as a parameter, which is what makes the new test independent of the time it runs at; see [GitHub's rate limit documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/using-the-rest-api/rate-limits-for-the-rest-api) for the headers involved."
        },
